## Summary

Implemented **`DET.MOTION.NO_AUTO_PLAY_FLASH`** as a deterministic accessibility check aligned with WCAG 2.3.1’s general flash limit (more than **3 flashes per second** for a simple on/off cycle).

### What changed

1. **`design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-motion-no-auto-play-flash.check.js`**
   - Exports `rule` and `run(ctx)` (findings array).
   - **`collectMotionNoAutoPlayFlashReport(page)`** scans the live DOM for:
     - **Fast infinite animations** — cycle &lt; ~0.67s (estimated &gt; 3 Hz for a 0↔1 toggle).
     - **Risky names** — `blink`, `flash`, `strobe`, `seizure`, `flicker` on computed `animation-name` or `@keyframes`.
     - **Autoplay video** — visible `video[autoplay]` (warn; may include rapid luminance change).
   - Skips near-zero durations when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is active (KS-style overrides).
   - **`findingsFromMotionNoAutoPlayFlashReport`** maps violations to standard finding fields (`severity`, `area`, `message`, `evidence`, `remediation`).
   - Supports precomputed `metrics.motionNoAutoPlayFlashReport` or on-demand Playwright collection.

2. **`design-rules/blender/rule-mappings.js`**
   - Registered under **`DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS`** as `implemented`:
     - `area`: `accessibility`
     - `scoreDimension`: `accessibilitySemanticsMeta`
     - `defaultSeverity`: `major`
     - `priorityWeight`: `9`

3. **`auditor-tests/det-motion-no-auto-play-flash.test.js`**
   - Unit tests for parsers, flash-rate math, finding mapping, and `run()`.

### Why this approach

The source rule allows **pixel sampling** with a manual fallback. This implementation uses **measurable CSS/DOM signals** (animation timing, keyframe names, autoplay video) so the check stays deterministic and cheap. Full luminance flash detection would need screenshot sampling and is left as a future extension.

